Now, we will edit the mkinitcpio preset file(s). Each preset file corresponds to
an installed kernel, allowing configuration on a per-kernel based. Further
"sub-presets" may be specified in the file. By default, this only includes
"default" and "fallback". Configuration for both these "sub-presets" is done in
a single preset file.

You can set the path to the generated image file (*_image=) as well as the path
to the final UKI (*_uki=) - which packages the image - in the preset file. The
*_options variable also allows specifying additional settings that will be
passed as parameters to mkinitcpio when building the preset. If you know what
you are doing, you can also override a lot of the default options set in
mkinitcpio.conf here.

In general however, no further editing of the presets should be needed at this
point. You can comment out the default_options line if you would like to
suppress the splash boot image. You could also specify a different save path
for the UKI, if you really wanted to. However, be aware that the boot loader
(systemd-boot) will only create entries automatically for images located under
/EFI/Linux on your EFI system partition. If you put them in a different
location, you will have to create the corresponding entries manually.
